text.en:
The so-called “punishment” contains one of the following four meanings, or their arbitrary combination.

These four meanings are:
(1) Something that is different from the dominant power;
(2) Something that cannot be fully explained by the rationale of enlightenment;
(3) Something contrary to the “universal” “main” “centre”;
(4) What keeps a distance from the formal system.

What kind of subject is folklore? Let's get down to business.

Folklore refers to the study of “people” (human beings, people) from a “common” perspective. In my view, the term “comfort” contains one of the four meanings described below, or any combination of them. These four meanings are:
(1) Something that is different from the dominant power;
(2) Something that cannot be fully explained by the rationale of enlightenment;
(3) Something contrary to the “universal” “main” “centre”;
(4) What keeps a distance from the formal system. The title of the book, “vernacular”, is a popular English expression.

text.zh:
“东村”可以是潮汕任何一个村子，或者说中国任何一个村子，全球任何一个村子都没什么两样，它是商品的世界。“新妇”可以是任何一个普通村子里的一群会哭泣的强壮女人如何寻找生存的门道的干过的所有奇葩事。



东村新妇实验剧团延续潮剧团的实践，“山寨”是我们的工作方法：透過持续行走、公开招募、临时搭建舞台与在地合作，让创作在不同地点与社群中生成——搭台、演出、用自带炉灶做饭、睡通铺。而剧团成员的身份也是多重的，控偶师兼木工、乐手兼司机、写作者兼厨师...与这样的表演实践平行运转的，是我们维持生存的“漂流经济模型”。每至一地，我们便通过在地工作坊、手工艺品销售及演出，建立即时的收入循环。模型以透明的成本收益分割为基础，确保所有参与女性的劳动被看见，并直接获得经济回报。“东村新妇”的梦想是诞生一个小小的舞台，过家家， 弄假成真，真正的漂流起来。



&nbsp;

&nbsp;

text.en:
“East Village” could be any village in the tide, or any village in China, and no village in the world could be different. A “new woman” can be all the strange things that a group of crying strong women in any village have done to find a way to survive.



In the East Village Experimental Women's Theatre, which continues the practice of the Tide Theatre, the "Campaign" is our method of work: through continuous walk, open recruitment, temporary stage-building and local cooperation, creativity is created in different places and communities - to set up stage, perform, cook with their own stoves, and sleep well. And the character of the troupe is multiple, and the puppets and carpenters, musicians and drivers, writers and cooks... are running in parallel with such performances as our survival “drive economy model”. Every place, we create an immediate income cycle through local workshops, handicraft sales and performances. The model is based on transparent cost-benefit splits to ensure that all women involved are seen and receive direct economic returns. East Village New Woman's dream is to have a little stage, to go home, to fake it, to really drift.



&nbsp;

